\section{Layouts}{

\code{layout} decides what a row is:
\itemize{
\item \code{"records"}: the input's rows, with search, sort and cell colors
(\code{shadings}, \code{color}). With \code{by}, rows sit under one collapsible header
per level. A finished table from R code (a structured or annotated data
frame, see \code{\link[=as_annotated_df]{as_annotated_df()}}) is drawn as it comes.
\item \code{"groups"}: one row per level of \code{by} (or one row without it), one
column per entry of \code{summaries}: counts and statistics as numbers, bars,
dots, boxes, point ranges, sparklines or spans.
\item \code{"variables"}: a Table 1. One row per statistic or level of each
variable in \code{summaries}, one column per level of \code{by}, with \code{stats},
\code{sections} and a \code{total} column.
}

\code{look} draws any layout as a \code{"table"}, a \code{"compact"} matrix (rotated
column titles, tiles as a heatmap) or \code{"cards"} (one card per summary in
groups, per column in records).
}

\section{Clicks}{

A click filters only when \code{drill} is set. In records it names the column
a click filters on, or \code{"auto"}; in groups and variables \code{"auto"} filters
on the clicked row's groups. With \code{drill_target} set, a click is sent to
that filter block instead, and the table keeps no selection of its own.
}

\section{Older code and boards}{

Argument names of blockr.viz before 0.3.0 (\code{value}, \code{group}, \code{pct_of},
\code{axis}, ...) still work in code, with a warning. Boards saved with the
table, tile and summary blocks restore as table blocks. A value an
argument does not take is an error. Any other name is kept as a block
attribute, for blockr.core and other packages (blockr.dock's \code{visible}).
}

